  "html": "<div class=\"postArticle-content js-postField js-notesSource editable\" id=\"editor_7\" g_editable=\"true\" role=\"textbox\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-default-value=\"Title\nTell your story…\"><section name=\"cb4a\" class=\"section section--body section--first section--last is-withGrafSelection\"><div class=\"section-divider\"><hr class=\"section-divider\"></div><div class=\"section-content\"><div class=\"section-inner sectionLayout--insetColumn\"><h3 name=\"af17\" class=\"graf graf--h3 graf--leading graf--title is-selected\" data-testid=\"editorTitleParagraph\">ECG-EKG (Electrocardiograph)</h3><p data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\" name=\"b719\" class=\"graf graf--p graf-after--h3\">For a university course project, we built an ECG circuit to amplify the heart's electrical activity and display it on an oscilloscope. This article walks through the amplification and filtering stages, with photographs and outputs from that project.</p><h4 data-testid=\"editorHeadingText\" name=\"6b74\" class=\"graf graf--h4 graf-after--p\">What is&nbsp;EKG?</h4><p data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\" name=\"8c80\" class=\"graf graf--p graf-after--h4\">An electrocardiogram (ECG, also called EKG) records the heart's electrical activity over time. Electrodes on the skin pick up small differences in electrical potential, which appear as a waveform.</p><figure tabindex=\"0\" contenteditable=\"false\" data-testid=\"editorImageParagraph\" name=\"d44a\" class=\"graf graf--figure graf-after--p is-defaultValue\"><div class=\"aspectRatioPlaceholder is-locked\" style=\"max-width: 320px; max-height: 244px;\"><div class=\"aspectRatioPlaceholder-fill\" style=\"padding-bottom: 76.3%;\"></div><img class=\"graf-image\" data-image-id=\"0*zOQZV-vQmKluQfRZ.jpeg\" data-width=\"320\" data-height=\"244\" data-is-featured=\"true\" src=\"https://cdn-images-1.medium.com/max/1600/0*zOQZV-vQmKluQfRZ.jpeg\"><div class=\"crosshair u-ignoreBlock\"></div></div><figcaption class=\"imageCaption\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-default-value=\"Type caption for image (optional)\"><span class=\"defaultValue\">Type caption for image (optional)</span><br></figcaption></figure><h4 data-testid=\"editorHeadingText\" name=\"288e\" class=\"graf graf--h4 graf-after--figure\">How Does It&nbsp;Work?</h4><p data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\" name=\"f732\" class=\"graf graf--p graf-after--h4\">ECG electrodes do not contain microphones or convert heart sounds into electrical signals. They detect electrical potential differences at the body surface. The measurement circuit amplifies and filters those signals. Recording heart sounds is a different measurement.</p><figure tabindex=\"0\" contenteditable=\"false\" data-testid=\"editorImageParagraph\" name=\"d0a7\" class=\"graf graf--figure graf-after--p is-defaultValue\"><div class=\"aspectRatioPlaceholder is-locked\" style=\"max-width: 320px; max-height: 209px;\"><div class=\"aspectRatioPlaceholder-fill\" style=\"padding-bottom: 65.3%;\"></div><img class=\"graf-image\" data-image-id=\"0*pH6_Ov1WCwngkKzR.gif\" data-width=\"320\" data-height=\"209\" src=\"https://cdn-images-1.medium.com/max/1600/0*pH6_Ov1WCwngkKzR.gif\"><div class=\"crosshair u-ignoreBlock\"></div></div><figcaption class=\"imageCaption\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-default-value=\"Type caption for image (optional)\"><span class=\"defaultValue\">Type caption for image (optional)</span><br></figcaption></figure><h4 data-testid=\"editorHeadingText\" name=\"abdc\" class=\"graf graf--h4 graf-after--figure\">Acquiring the EKG&nbsp;Signal</h4><p data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\" name=\"4d16\" class=\"graf graf--p graf-after--h4\">Our project used three electrodes attached to the two arms and one leg. Electrode count is not the same as lead count: an ECG lead represents a particular view of electrical activity. Our aim was to amplify a small voltage difference and observe it on an oscilloscope.</p><figure tabindex=\"0\" contenteditable=\"false\" data-testid=\"editorImageParagraph\" name=\"ecd1\" class=\"graf graf--figure graf-after--p is-defaultValue\"><div class=\"aspectRatioPlaceholder is-locked\" style=\"max-width: 640px; max-height: 364px;\"><div class=\"aspectRatioPlaceholder-fill\" style=\"padding-bottom: 56.89999999999999%;\"></div><img class=\"graf-image\" data-image-id=\"0*el4wHvik-H8lwXuO.jpeg\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"364\" src=\"https://cdn-images-1.medium.com/max/1600/0*el4wHvik-H8lwXuO.jpeg\"><div class=\"crosshair u-ignoreBlock\"></div></div><figcaption class=\"imageCaption\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-default-value=\"Type caption for image (optional)\"><span class=\"defaultValue\">Type caption for image (optional)</span><br></figcaption></figure><p data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\" name=\"32b6\" class=\"graf graf--p graf-after--figure\">We amplified the voltage difference between the arm electrodes with an instrumentation amplifier; the leg electrode formed part of the circuit's reference connection. Instead of using an AD624, we built the amplifier stage from operational amplifiers and resistors. This let us examine the amplification stage as part of the coursework.</p><figure tabindex=\"0\" contenteditable=\"false\" data-testid=\"editorImageParagraph\" name=\"c128\" class=\"graf graf--figure graf-after--p is-defaultValue\"><div class=\"aspectRatioPlaceholder is-locked\" style=\"max-width: 640px; max-height: 310px;\"><div class=\"aspectRatioPlaceholder-fill\" style=\"padding-bottom: 48.4%;\"></div><img class=\"graf-image\" data-image-id=\"0*3GrSAMzjWfORvGtt.jpeg\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"310\" src=\"https://cdn-images-1.medium.com/max/1600/0*3GrSAMzjWfORvGtt.jpeg\"><div class=\"crosshair u-ignoreBlock\"></div></div><figcaption class=\"imageCaption\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-default-value=\"Type caption for image (optional)\"><span class=\"defaultValue\">Type caption for image (optional)</span><br></figcaption></figure><p data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\" name=\"cb0a\" class=\"graf graf--p graf-after--figure\">The amplified signal can include baseline drift and noise as well as the ECG waveform. We used a band-pass filter to reduce unwanted components. ECG is not a single-frequency signal: the lower and upper cutoff frequencies need to preserve the waveform features being studied. Narrowing the passband too far can distort those features.</p><figure tabindex=\"0\" contenteditable=\"false\" data-testid=\"editorImageParagraph\" name=\"0443\" class=\"graf graf--figure graf-after--p\"><div class=\"aspectRatioPlaceholder is-locked\" style=\"max-width: 640px; max-height: 480px;\"><div class=\"aspectRatioPlaceholder-fill\" style=\"padding-bottom: 75%;\"></div><img class=\"graf-image\" data-image-id=\"0*YEJh7_r0DBqvJZmf.jpeg\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"480\" src=\"https://cdn-images-1.medium.com/max/1600/0*YEJh7_r0DBqvJZmf.jpeg\"><div class=\"crosshair u-ignoreBlock\"></div></div><figcaption class=\"imageCaption\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-default-value=\"Type caption for image (optional)\">Unfiltered signals</figcaption></figure><p data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\" name=\"b867\" class=\"graf graf--p graf-after--figure\">We also encountered 50 Hz mains interference and used a notch filter to reduce it. This suppresses a narrow frequency band around 50 Hz. Making that band too wide can also affect ECG components in the same range.</p><p data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\" name=\"2ae4\" class=\"graf graf--p graf-after--p\">Here is the screen capture of the ISIS diagram of the circuit we designed to acquire, filter, and amplify the EKG signal.</p><figure tabindex=\"0\" contenteditable=\"false\" data-testid=\"editorImageParagraph\" name=\"339c\" class=\"graf graf--figure graf-after--p is-defaultValue\"><div class=\"aspectRatioPlaceholder is-locked\" style=\"max-width: 614px; max-height: 357px;\"><div class=\"aspectRatioPlaceholder-fill\" style=\"padding-bottom: 58.099999999999994%;\"></div><img class=\"graf-image\" data-image-id=\"0*qgjsYgLzdVVGCwRU.jpeg\" data-width=\"614\" data-height=\"357\" src=\"https://cdn-images-1.medium.com/max/1600/0*qgjsYgLzdVVGCwRU.jpeg\"><div class=\"crosshair u-ignoreBlock\"></div></div><figcaption class=\"imageCaption\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-default-value=\"Type caption for image (optional)\"><span class=\"defaultValue\">Type caption for image (optional)</span><br></figcaption></figure><p data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\" name=\"e734\" class=\"graf graf--p graf-after--figure\">I wanted to share with you some images from our work environment and some outputs we obtained during our studies.</p><figure tabindex=\"0\" contenteditable=\"false\" data-testid=\"editorImageParagraph\" name=\"a975\" class=\"graf graf--figure graf-after--p is-defaultValue\"><div class=\"aspectRatioPlaceholder is-locked\" style=\"max-width: 640px; max-height: 478px;\"><div class=\"aspectRatioPlaceholder-fill\" style=\"padding-bottom: 74.7%;\"></div><img class=\"graf-image\" data-image-id=\"0*DNsH8h8WwKX_r8iW.jpeg\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"478\" src=\"https://cdn-images-1.medium.com/max/1600/0*DNsH8h8WwKX_r8iW.jpeg\"><div class=\"crosshair u-ignoreBlock\"></div></div><figcaption class=\"imageCaption\" contenteditable=\"true\" data-default-value=\"Type caption for image (optional)\"><span class=\"defaultValue\">Type caption for image (optional)</span><br></figcaption></figure><ul class=\"postList\"><li data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\" name=\"3004\" class=\"graf graf--li graf-after--figure\">Image 1: Materials used in the making of the EKG. As seen, it’s just a handful of components.</li><li data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\" name=\"8bb3\" class=\"graf graf--li graf-after--li\">Image 2: The printed circuit board of our EKG device.</li><li data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\" name=\"38fb\" class=\"graf graf--li graf-after--li\">Image 3: The first test run of our circuit on the board.</li><li data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\" name=\"652c\" class=\"graf graf--li graf-after--li\">Image 4 and result: Our output signal as shown in the image.</li></ul><p data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\" name=\"41df\" class=\"graf graf--p graf-after--li\">We observed the circuit's output on an oscilloscope. Displaying it through a microcontroller would require analog-to-digital conversion, with a suitable sampling rate, resolution, and input range. Seeing a waveform on the oscilloscope did not establish clinical accuracy or validate the circuit's safety for use on people.</p><h4 data-testid=\"editorHeadingText\" name=\"3fac\" class=\"graf graf--h4 graf-after--p\">Note</h4><p name=\"7291\" class=\"graf graf--p graf-after--h4 graf--trailing\" data-testid=\"editorParagraphText\">This is a record of an undergraduate project, not a validated medical-device design or a construction guide for use on people. Measurements on people require equipment with appropriate patient protection and isolation. Updated October 9, 2026 to correct the explanation of ECG sensing and filtering. Sources: <a href=\"https://medium.com/r/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nhs.uk%2Ftests-and-treatments%2Felectrocardiogram%2F\" data-href=\"https://medium.com/r/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nhs.uk%2Ftests-and-treatments%2Felectrocardiogram%2F\" class=\"markup--anchor markup--p-anchor\" rel=\"noopener\" data-tooltip=\"https://medium.com/r/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nhs.uk%2Ftests-and-treatments%2Felectrocardiogram%2F\" data-tooltip-position=\"bottom\" data-tooltip-type=\"link\" target=\"_blank\">NHS: what an ECG records</a>; <a href=\"https://medium.com/r/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fez.analog.com%2Famplifiers%2Fa%2Fdocuments%2FDO10157%2Ffilter-requirements-for-ad8232\" data-href=\"https://medium.com/r/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fez.analog.com%2Famplifiers%2Fa%2Fdocuments%2FDO10157%2Ffilter-requirements-for-ad8232\" class=\"markup--anchor markup--p-anchor\" rel=\"noopener\" data-tooltip=\"https://medium.com/r/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fez.analog.com%2Famplifiers%2Fa%2Fdocuments%2FDO10157%2Ffilter-requirements-for-ad8232\" data-tooltip-position=\"bottom\" data-tooltip-type=\"link\" target=\"_blank\">Analog Devices: ECG filter requirements</a>.</p></div></div></section></div><div class=\"u-sm-hide u-absolute u-marginRight30 u-textColorNormal u-fontSize14 u-textAlignRight\" style=\"top: 23px; right: 1206.5px; height: 68.5px;\"><div class=\"u-absolute u-left14 u-top0 u-width1 u-height100pct u-overflowHidden\"><div class=\"js-labelBar u-borderRightLighter u-transition--transform125 u-height100pct u-absolute u-topNegative100Percent\" style=\"transform: translate3d(0px, 68.5px, 0px);\"></div></div><div class=\"js-titleLabel u-paddingTop19 u-absolute u-top0 u-right0 u-transition--transform200Spring u-transition--fadeIn200Delay150\" style=\"transform: translate3d(0px, 0px, 0px);\">Title</div><div class=\"js-subtitleLabel u-paddingTop11 u-absolute u-top0 u-right0 u-transition--transform200Spring u-transition--fadeOut100\">Subtitle</div><div class=\"js-kickerLabel u-paddingTop4 u-absolute u-top0 u-right0 u-transition--transform200Spring u-transition--fadeOut100\">Kicker</div></div><div class=\"inlineTooltip buttonScalableGroup\" style=\"\"><button class=\"button button--small button--circle button--dark button--withChrome u-baseColor--buttonDark button--withIcon button--withSvgIcon button--inlineTooltipControl js-inlineTooltipControl\" title=\"Add an image, video, embed, or new part\" aria-label=\"Add an image, video, embed, or new part\" data-action=\"inline-menu\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-testid=\"editorAddButton\"><span class=\"svgIcon svgIcon--addMediaPlus svgIcon--25px\"><svg class=\"svgIcon-use\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\"><path d=\"M20 12h-7V5h-1v7H5v1h7v7h1v-7h7\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\"></path></svg></span></button><div class=\"inlineTooltip-menu\"><button class=\"button button--small button--circle button--dark button--withChrome u-baseColor--buttonDark button--withIcon button--withSvgIcon button--scale u-transitionSeries button--chromeless\" title=\"Add an image\" aria-label=\"Add an image\" data-action=\"inline-menu-im